diff --git a/docs/MODULES_REFERENCE.md b/docs/MODULES_REFERENCE.md
index 7ee551ec..967fc873 100644
--- a/docs/MODULES_REFERENCE.md
+++ b/docs/MODULES_REFERENCE.md
@@ -230,6 +230,41 @@ All filesystem operations translate PS3 paths (e.g., `/dev_hdd0/game/NPUA80001/`
 - Sixaxis motion sensor data (accelerometer X/Y/Z, gyroscope)
 - Rumble/vibration motor control (small/large motor)
 
+**Xbox / XInput button mapping (Windows):** same positions as on a DualShock 3.
+
+| Xbox | PS3 | Notes |
+|---|---|---|
+| A / B / X / Y | Cross / Circle / Square / Triangle | pressure 255 when pressed |
+| LB / RB | L1 / R1 | |
+| LT / RT | L2 / R2 | digital past 30/255 (`XINPUT_GAMEPAD_TRIGGER_THRESHOLD`); pressure word = the trigger value |
+| LS / RS click | L3 / R3 | |
+| View (Back) | Select | |
+| Menu (Start) | Start | |
+| D-pad, left/right stick | D-pad, left/right stick | stick deadzone 7849 (`XINPUT_GAMEPAD_LEFT_THUMB_DEADZONE`), rescaled to 1..255, centre 128, Y up = low |
+
+XInput user slot *n* is PS3 port *n*; a connected/disconnected pad is picked up on the next poll (hot-plug, polled at most every 4 ms).
+Port 0 is always reported connected (a virtual pad, idle sticks at 128) so titles waiting for a controller boot.
+
+**Remapping: `PS3_PAD_MAP`** (read once at `cellPadInit`; unset = the table above):
+
+```
+PS3_PAD_MAP="<xbox>=<ps3>[,<xbox>=<ps3>...]"
+  xbox: A B X Y LB RB LT RT LS RS (L3 R3) BACK (VIEW) START (MENU) UP DOWN LEFT RIGHT (DPAD_UP ...)
+  ps3:  CROSS CIRCLE SQUARE TRIANGLE L1 R1 L2 R2 L3 R3 SELECT START UP DOWN LEFT RIGHT NONE
+```
+
+Only the listed sources change; names are case-insensitive; several sources may drive one PS3 button; `NONE` unbinds.
+Pressure follows the source (a trigger gives its analog value, a button 255). Unparsable entries are logged
+(`[cellPad] PS3_PAD_MAP: cannot parse ...`) and skipped. Examples:
+
+```
+set PS3_PAD_MAP=A=circle,B=cross                 rem confirm/back swapped (Japanese layout)
+set PS3_PAD_MAP=LT=l1,RT=r1,LB=l2,RB=r2          rem triggers and bumpers swapped
+```
+
+The mapping is tested without a controller by `libs/input/tests/pad_map_test.c` (build line in the file).
+The SDL2 backend keeps its fixed GameController mapping (no `PS3_PAD_MAP`).
+
 **Key Functions:**
 - `cellPadInit(max_ports)` — initialize pad system
 - `cellPadGetData(port, &data)` — poll controller state
