+ * PS3_AVSYNC_LOG=<prefix>: A/V sync probe (diagnostic; off by default, costs
+ * one getenv when off). Answers "when is a given guest sample actually heard?":
+ *   <prefix>.audio.bin   one record per mixed block of every running 2-channel
+ *                        port (movie audio; the 8-channel FMOD port is left
+ *                        out): av_block_hdr + the block as 256 stereo host
+ *                        floats (before the port level). dev_frame = index of
+ *                        the block's first frame in the device stream.
+ *   <prefix>.clock.csv   device clock: qpc_us,pos_frames,qpcpos_us,padding --
+ *                        IAudioClock position (what the speakers play) at a
+ *                        QPC time, so dev_frame -> heard-at time is a lookup.
+ *   <prefix>.events.csv  qpc_us,event,port,read_index (open/start/stop/close,
+ *                        stream (re)open)
+ * Times are QPC microseconds, the base rsx_live_draw's PS3_AVSYNC_LOG present
+ * log uses (tools: work\avsync\avsync.py in thp8-native). */
+typedef struct {
+    u32 magic;          /* 'AVA1' */
+    u32 port;
+    u64 qpc_us;         /* when the block was mixed */
+    u64 dev_frame;      /* first frame of the block in the device stream */
+    u64 read_index;     /* port block counter before this block */
