+ * Several installs and versions of a port can use one save folder, and two of them can run at the same time.
+ * <root>/.ps3recomp-savedata.lock carries two byte-range locks far past its end (its text stays readable):
+ *   SESSION  held by a game from its first save-data call to its exit. The OS drops it when the process ends, crash
+ *            or kill included, so it is never stale. Taken without waiting: when another game holds it, both use the
+ *            folder and this is logged (the launcher warns before it starts a second game on the same folder).
+ *   PASS     held for one save or load pass, and for the import: passes of two games never interleave, so a load
