+ * Inline guest memory access for lifted code built with ppu_lifter.py
+ * --opt-fast-mem (tools/ppu_codegen_opt.py).
+ *
+ * Such code loads/stores vm_base + addr itself and only calls the vm_read* /
+ * vm_write* helpers above when ppu_line_flags[addr >> 7] says so (bit0 loads,
+ * bit1 stores; one byte per 128-byte line, runtime/spu/spu_coherency.c). So
+ * every line where the helpers do something besides the plain access has to
+ * be flagged:
+ *   - lines an SPU has reserved (stores; set by spu_coherency.c itself);
+ *   - the null page: stores below 0x1000 are dropped/reported (vm_null_store),
+ *     reads below 0x10000 are reported ([null-read]);
+ *   - each raw SPU's problem-state window (spu_raw_is_reg: mailbox pops, run
+ *     control, signal notification, proxy DMA), loads and stores;
+ *   - the GCM label/control page [VM_HLE_INJECT_BASE, +0x3000): labels, put/get/ref
+ *     (read32 of ref publishes a fence, GCM_REFPOLL), the FIFO callback sentinel;
+ *   - every line, for stores, while PS3_NULL_SWEEP contains a sweep;
+ *   - every line when a read or write diagnostic is armed (PPU_RWATCH,
+ *     PPU_WWATCH, PPU_WVAL, PPU_FORCE_READ_ADDR, ...) or PPU_MEM_SLOW=1, and on
+ *     a POSIX build (ppu_vm_size != 0: the helpers do the real range check).
+ * NOT covered, by design: the default-on [HOTREAD] spin reports are
+ * diagnostics only -- set PPU_MEM_SLOW=1 to get them back.
