+/* Point the exe's own IAT entry for the CRT's getenv at cached_getenv. Every
+ * getenv call in the image -- `call [__imp_getenv]` from dllimport'ed headers
+ * and the `getenv` jmp thunk alike -- loads its target from that one slot, so
+ * this is the run-time equivalent of the MSVC slot definition above. Only the
+ * exe is patched; getenv calls made inside other DLLs (ucrtbase itself, D3D,
+ * drivers) keep the OS lookup, exactly as on MSVC.
+ * Matches imports BY NAME from the UCRT environment API set (zig/MinGW-w64
+ * UCRT links api-ms-win-crt-environment-l1-1-0.dll), ucrtbase.dll, or
+ * msvcrt.dll (an msvcrt-flavoured MinGW). Returns the number of slots patched;
+ * GETENV_STATS=1 also logs it. */
+static int ppu_getenv_iat_patch(void)
