+ * kernel transitions cost about as much CPU as a short spin. So spin up to
+ * SPU_CH_SPIN_US (default 20; 0 disables) re-checking the channel before
+ * sleeping -- but only where waits ARE short: per host thread, a history of
+ * the last 8 waits, and the spin runs while at least half of them ended within
+ * the spin budget. While it does not, every 16th wait spins anyway as a probe,
+ * so a thread whose waits turn short starts spinning again (a wait that slept
