+# ps3recomp web build (WebAssembly + WebGPU)
+
+Status: milestone 1 (feasibility). The folder layout below is the target; nothing in it is game-specific
+except `config.json` and `data/`, which a port generates from the player's own game files.
+
+## Source (2026-10-24: one runtime line)
+
+The browser build is built from the same ps3recomp line as the Windows and Linux ports (`thp8-unified`, taken by the
+release as its next runtime): browser-only code sits behind `PS3_WASM` / `__EMSCRIPTEN__`, browser-only files
+(`libs/filesystem/web_vfs.c`, `libs/input/web_input.c`, `libs/video/webgpu/`, `runtime/platform/ps3_wasm_*.c`) are
+not part of the native CMake library, and the Windows build is preprocess-identical to the release runtime it was
+merged onto. The P8Plus plugin is compiled from the plugin repository's master sources with its
+`native/p8plus_plugin/web/` glue. Until then the browser build was an object-level composite of several web branches
+(rt25 = thp8-wasm + thp8-wasm-bytes, 47 runtime commits behind the release). Build script: thp8-native
+`work/webunify/build_u.sh <tag>` (Emscripten 4.0.23, idle priority, waits on the machine's run flags).
+
+## The portable folder
+
+```
+www/
+  index.html, boot.js, *.js     JS host (capability checks, workers, VFS, input, audio)
+  <title>.wasm(.br)             the port (lifted code + runtime), built locally from the player's own game
+  config.json                   title name, wasm file, options (relative paths only)
+  data/index.json               file list of the packed game data (sizes; used for range fetches + cache keys)
+  data/files/...                the game files, packed by tools/mkdata.py from the player's own dump
+  _headers                      COOP/COEP rules for static hosts that read them
+serve.exe / serve-macos-* / serve-linux-*   the launcher (one static binary per OS, ~25-95 KB)
+```
+
+Everything uses relative paths, so the folder can be copied to another machine as a whole.
+Game data is fetched in byte ranges on demand and cached in the browser (OPFS), so a device downloads only what
+it plays. The Bink movies (most of the size) stream the same way.
+
+## Running it on this machine
+
+```
+serve            (Windows: double-click serve.exe, or run it from a terminal)
+./serve-linux-x64
+./serve-macos-arm64        (macOS may need: xattr -d com.apple.quarantine serve-macos-arm64)
+```
+
+Then open http://localhost:8080/ in Chrome or Edge. Options: `--port N`, `--dir DIR`, `--open` (opens the browser).
+By default the launcher listens on 127.0.0.1 only: no other device can reach it.
+
+### Mods (your own mods folder, served in place)
+
+The browser build reads mods the same way the native port does: a mods folder (data packs that overlay game files,
+the P8Plus plugin's `plugins/thp8_mod_p8plus.ini`, ...) mounted at `/mods`. Nothing is copied: index the folder once
+and let the launcher serve it straight from where it lives.
+
+```
+python tools/mkdata.py --folder "<your mods folder>" --name mods_p8plus --out <index folder> --mode index \
+       --exclude "plugins/*.dll" --exclude "_p8plus_cap/*"
+serve --dir <www> --mount /mods_p8plus=<index folder>/mods_p8plus --mount /mods_p8plus/files=<your mods folder>
+```
+
+Then open the page with `?mods=p8plus`. `--mount /URL/PREFIX=PATH` serves a folder (or one file) read-only, with
+`Cache-Control: no-store`, and the page never stores mods files in browser storage either (they are fetched on
+demand and held only in a small in-memory cache), so private content such as your own music stays on your PC
+and the browser profile does not grow. Folders named `*.cap_stage` and folder links are never indexed or served.
+With a mods folder the HD texture packs are on (1 GB budget; `?PS3_TEXREPL=0` turns them off). What else works
+and what does not yet: see "Parity with the native Project 8 Plus" below.
+
+## Why it needs special headers
+
+The port runs on several threads (Web Workers sharing memory). Browsers allow shared memory only on pages that are
+*cross-origin isolated* and served from a *secure context*:
+
+* Headers `Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin` and `Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp` (the launcher
+  sends them; `_headers` carries them for static hosts that read that file).
+* A secure context: `https://...` or `http://localhost`. A plain `http://192.168.x.y:8080` LAN address is **not**
+  secure, so threads (and the game) will not start there.
+
+## Opening it from your other devices (your choice; nothing here is set up automatically)
+
+Pick one. Each of these exposes the folder beyond this PC, so only do it on networks and devices you trust.
+
+1. **Private tunnel with HTTPS (recommended).** A mesh VPN such as Tailscale can serve a local port over HTTPS
+   inside your private tailnet only (`tailscale serve 8080`). Your devices then open the `https://<pc>.<tailnet>.ts.net`
+   address. Secure context and headers both work; nothing is published to the internet.
+2. **LAN with a browser exception.** Start the launcher with `--host 0.0.0.0` (or this PC's LAN IP); Windows may ask
+   to allow it through the firewall. On the other device, Chrome/Edge can treat that one address as secure:
+   `chrome://flags/#unsafely-treat-insecure-origin-as-secure` -> add `http://<pc-ip>:8080`, relaunch. Works on desktop
+   Chrome and Android Chrome; not on iPhone/iPad.
+3. **LAN with HTTPS.** Put a local HTTPS reverse proxy (e.g. Caddy with its local CA) in front of the launcher and
+   install that CA on your devices. More setup, but works on every device, iPhone/iPad included.
+
+## Browser support (target)
+
+| Browser | Status |
+|---|---|
+| Chrome / Edge (desktop) | primary target: WebGPU, wasm threads, tail calls, 4 GB memory |
+| Firefox (desktop) | should work where its WebGPU is enabled |
+| Safari (macOS 26+) | WebGPU available; wasm feature set to be checked |
+| Steam Deck (Chrome/Firefox in desktop mode) | desktop-class; expected to work |
+| Phones / tablets | not yet: the port needs a 4 GB WebAssembly memory today; a compacted memory map is planned |
+
+The start page checks all of this and says what is missing instead of failing silently.
+
+## Parity with the native Project 8 Plus
+
+State of the browser build (default page, 2026-10-14) against the native P8Plus port. "Gate" = checked against the
+native port in the same scene (pictures) and measured as the median of 3+ browser boots per side.
+
+| Feature | Browser | Notes |
+|---|---|---|
+| P8Plus plugin (60 fps, menus60, widescreen math, bloom / grading / DoF, draw distance) | yes | same plugin source as native, built in |
+| Skip intro (`skip_intro` on / off, press to skip) | yes (rt11+, default rt25) | gate W (`rt11intro`): `skip_intro = on` skips the logos and reaches the main menu (frame); with it off, Enter, pad A or a click each cut both logos ("movie cut" x2 per boot). The first boot builds the game's data cache (main menu about 70 s after Start); every later launch is warm: main menu 11.4 s after Start (gate WM `rt12wm`; rt12w and later; rt22 10.9 s, default rt25). If loading ever stops for 20 s, a "Stuck loading" box offers Reload / Reload without cache / Save log (3 stalls were seen in warm boots on 2026-10-15 before this; none in the 54 warm boots after) |
+| Mods folder overlay (boot screens, smoothed skater / head models, soundtrack) | yes, `?mods=p8plus` | served from your folder in place, never stored by the browser; boot screens gated; smoothed models cost about 2% fps |
+| HD texture packs | yes, on with mods | gated at render scale "high": visible match with native, fps within noise, about +105 MB VRAM |
+| Render scale, FXAA, supersampling, sharpen (`[renderer]` / `PS3_GFX_*`) | yes; from the mods folder's ini (P8Plus default "high") or `PS3_GFX_*` | native present pass; gated: matches native, no fps cost with command-list kicks off (browser default); about +660 MB VRAM at "high" |
+| Create-a-Skater Plus (colours, items, body / face shape, preview) | yes (rt11+, default rt25), screens gated | gate Z2 (`rt12cas`) vs native: CHOOSE YOUR STYLE lineup with normal faces (head default colour dropped, no blue face), HATS list with the BEANIE previewed on focus; module on (5 hooks), 0 guest-memory failures. The colour and body / face shape menus run the same plugin code but were not shot-checked |
+| CAS mod items | yes | gate Z2: the example HEADPHONES item from a mods folder is listed under MISC ITEMS and worn, as native |
+| CAS eye colour | yes (gated on rt12w = rt12 + the launch fix; same plugin) | gate CAS2 (`rt12cas2`): EYES > EYE COLOR swatch h210 s70 v100 gives blue irises with the whites kept, as native; the recoloured eye texture is written to `/hdd0/p8plus/_cas_plus` and shown through the texture redirect |
+| CAS looks save / load | yes (gated on rt12w; same plugin as rt12) | gate LS (`rt12ls`): SAVE LOOK shows "Saved" (look file in `/hdd0/p8plus/_cas_presets`, this site's storage); after a fresh page load LOAD LOOK lists "CLASSIC SKATER <date>" as native and loads it (17 parts) |
+| Camera invert saved | yes | in this site's storage (user settings file) |
