+  return {};
+}
+
+// Dev machine guard: flags.txt (work/wasm/tools/flagwatch.sh) says "clear" unless an exclusive perf turn or the
+// user's own game session is on. A run never starts then, and a running page stops itself (navigates to an inert
+// page, which ends every worker) within ~2 s of the flag appearing. No flags.txt (a player's own copy): no guard.
+// "userweb" (USER_WEB: the user plays this web build in their own browser) only stops automated ?measure pages: the
+// user's own page treats it as clear.
+const automated = new URLSearchParams(location.search).has("measure");
+// ?hirestimer=1 (wasm-perf 2026-10-15, experiment; default off): keep a 1 ms timer pending on this page's main thread.
+// Chrome then runs this renderer process at the 1 ms Windows timer resolution (it does so for pages with short
+// pending timers); otherwise a worker's timed Atomics.wait overshoots by up to the 15.6 ms default quantum, which made
+// the game's 1-4 ms usleeps (FileIO / Bink / FMOD threads) come back late and the 33 ms frames (PS3_WASM_LAT). The
+// timeout is re-armed from a MessageChannel message, so it never becomes a nested timer (no 4 ms clamp). No system
+// setting is touched. Cost: ~1000 tiny main-thread wakes/s.
+// Default (coordinator 2026-10-15): on for machines under 12 logical cores (they get sleep mode 0, see preRun:
+// +7.4% fps, half the >4 ms late sleeps, ~1/4 core); off on 12+ (sleep mode 3). ?hirestimer=0 / =1 overrides.
